      "title": "Modeling Inhibited Growth"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "79dfba0b-24db-5664-b4c9-d12274cb27d0",
      ":question/problem": "A laboratory incubator initially contains $21$ cultures, and its maximum capacity is $452$ cultures. Let $B(t)$ be the number of cultures, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in days. Its population obeys an inhibited growth model. The rate of increase equals $5$ times the difference between the maximum capacity and the current population. Which differential equation models this population?",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7875e0a1-7a16-5786-87e7-5a77a72087b1",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "f5d53b2e-c3cb-5b93-a2c6-a195e3fa68b9",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=-5(452-B)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c6f210f7-cd67-501d-8ec0-6733980138d9",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=(452-B)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "4eca7785-a388-51e6-9aa3-5140075ea5c2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=5(452-B)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "7e67d3b2-9f17-5e41-9731-8018a73dea2e",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=2260-B"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "20e3aa6b-07e8-5c44-a5d0-073bb9e6dafd",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=5(21-B)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "4eca7785-a388-51e6-9aa3-5140075ea5c2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate at which the number of cultures $B(t)$ in the laboratory incubator changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current number of cultures. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-B),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=452$ cultures, and $k=5$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=5(452-B).\n$$"
    },
