      ":question/worked-solution": "The rate at which the number of cultures $B(t)$ in the laboratory incubator changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the current number of cultures. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-B),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=452$ cultures, and $k=\\frac{2}{5}$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}B}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{2}{5}(452-B).\n$$"
    },
